[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3043868467","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108365#issuecomment-3043868467","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108365","id":3043868467,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61bb8z","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-07T07:55:40Z","updated_at":"2025-07-07T08:04:38Z","body":"Looks fine but the node selection shouldn't need to loop over the entire `EditorNode::get_singleton()->get_editor_selection()`.\r\n\r\nThe `MeshInstance3DEditorPlugin` already uses `Ref<MultiNodeEdit>`  for handling and editing multiple `MeshInstance3D`.\r\n\r\nThe problem is that it currently only picks a single `MeshInstance3D` node in the `edit()` function. So that should be changed instead of looping over the `EditorNode::get_singleton()->get_editor_selection()`.\r\n\r\nWould also allow all the other menu functions to work the same or to display a warning popup confirmation to users upfront that they are about to edit and change x-amount of nodes (... there are \"select-all\" users accidents and running those menu options on too many nodes will be incredibly slow and freeze the editor).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3043868467/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3044238365","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108365#issuecomment-3044238365","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108365","id":3044238365,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61c2Qd","user":{"login":"aryan-11825114","id":62866798,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyODY2Nzk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62866798?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114","html_url":"https://github.com/aryan-11825114","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-07T09:51:21Z","updated_at":"2025-07-07T09:51:21Z","body":"Honestly, I'm not quite sure I fully understand your explanation above as I'm very unfamiliar with the code, but I mainly tried to replicate how collision shapes are created, and regarding the editor freeze I tried unwrapping UV2 meshes of about 1000 mesh-instances and did not encounter any, I have a very old laptop with an i5-8300H and a GTX 1050ti","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3044238365/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3083508835","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108365#issuecomment-3083508835","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108365","id":3083508835,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc63ypxj","user":{"login":"Nodragem","id":10520249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIwMjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10520249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem","html_url":"https://github.com/Nodragem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-17T10:24:57Z","updated_at":"2025-07-17T10:26:52Z","body":"I think @smix8 is suggesting that we have a look at the function at line 686:\r\n```cpp\r\nvoid MeshInstance3DEditorPlugin::edit(Object *p_object) {\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tMeshInstance3D *mi = Object::cast_to<MeshInstance3D>(p_object);\r\n\t\tif (mi) {\r\n\t\t\tmesh_editor->edit(mi);\r\n\t\t\treturn;\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\tRef<MultiNodeEdit> mne = Ref<MultiNodeEdit>(p_object);\r\n\tNode *edited_scene = EditorNode::get_singleton()->get_edited_scene();\r\n\tif (mne.is_valid() && edited_scene) {\r\n\t\tfor (int i = 0; i < mne->get_node_count(); i++) {\r\n\t\t\tMeshInstance3D *mi = Object::cast_to<MeshInstance3D>(edited_scene->get_node(mne->get_node(i)));\r\n\t\t\tif (mi) {\r\n\t\t\t\tmesh_editor->edit(mi);\r\n\t\t\t\treturn;\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n\tmesh_editor->edit(nullptr);\r\n}\r\n```\r\nAs far as I can tell, this is already looping over multiple MeshInstance3Ds, and it assigns the first valid occurence to the variable `node` (i.e. mesh_editor.edit(mi)).\r\n\r\nThis `node` is then used by:\r\n- `MENU_OPTION_DEBUG_UV1`, \r\n- `MENU_OPTION_DEBUG_UV2`,\r\n- `MENU_OPTION_CREATE_UV2`, \r\n- `_create_outline_mesh()`, \r\n- `MENU_OPTION_CREATE_DEBUG_TANGENTS`, \r\n- `_create_navigation_mesh()`\r\nThey mostly use `node->get_mesh()` or similar and apply their function to it. Which means that they all don't support multi-selection.\r\n\r\nWe should note that the only function that supports multiselection is `_create_collision_shape()` and they use the same method as @aryan-11825114 used, that is `EditorNode::get_singleton()->get_editor_selection()`.\r\n\r\n@smix8 is suggesting to replace `node` with a list of nodes. This would mean:\r\n- keep a reference to `node` (and maybe rename it to `top_selected_mesh` ) so that all the code that is not supporting multiselection (i.e. above list) does not break,\r\n- use the new list of nodes (maybe we could name it `selected_meshes`) for `MENU_OPTION_CREATE_UV2`\r\n- use the new list of nodes for `_create_collision_shape()`\r\n\r\nI think we could:\r\n- accept this PR as it is, based on the fact that `_create_collision_shape()` used the same solution\r\n- open a new PR to refactor `node` into a list of nodes and adapt the code accordingly \r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3083508835/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3086693521","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108365#issuecomment-3086693521","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108365","id":3086693521,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc63-zSR","user":{"login":"aryan-11825114","id":62866798,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyODY2Nzk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62866798?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114","html_url":"https://github.com/aryan-11825114","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryan-11825114/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-18T04:36:43Z","updated_at":"2025-07-18T04:36:43Z","body":"Thanks for writing an explanation, maybe I could try to write a refactor later if its something I can do, but don't count on it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3086693521/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}